desc: Tap Dance (4ms Tapographic Delay port) by chmaha
tags: delay multitap rhythmic echo
author: chmaha
version: 1.1
changelog:
  Add full copyright and licence header (upstream authors' notices).
about:
  A tap-tempo multitap delay: tap a rhythm on the Tap pad (or send MIDI notes) and every tap becomes an echo, up to 32 taps.
  Edit switch: Add appends taps, Ins inserts them into the running loop, Off ignores taps. Time stretches the whole rhythm,
  Feedback repeats it, Modulation wobbles each tap, Morph sets the fade time between patterns.
  Six buttons recall the factory and saved rhythms (hold a button 1.2 s, then click it again to save); Delete removes the last
  tap, hold it to toggle Sync to the clock; Repeat loops the current pattern, hold it to clear all taps.
  MIDI: every note taps with its velocity, except the Repeat note (C2 by default), which works like the Repeat gate jack.
  Clock From Host sends one clock pulse per beat while the transport plays (for Sync and tap quantising).
  Ported from the 4ms Tapographic Delay module of 4ms CoreModules (MetaModule / VCV Rack, 4ms Company,
  https://github.com/4ms/metamodule-core-modules, GPLv3+), original Tapo firmware by Matthias Puech (MIT).
  JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license
  Claude generated some of this code
